This directory contains the OS-independent "common code" of the Intel ice
driver, imported from the FreeBSD main branch at git SHA
310145642312e1c5fb3d8efa8321cf905d0354c4 (sys/dev/ice).

OS adaptation lives in ../ice_osdep.h and ../ice_osdep.c and in the rest of
the driver.  All files in this directory are unmodified from that commit,
except the local changes listed below.

Files not compiled
------------------

These files were imported but are not in ICE_INTC_OBJS
(usr/src/uts/common/Makefile.files):

    ice_dcb.c		DCB/LLDP support.  Nothing else in the common code
			calls it; omitted until DCB is supported.
    ice_vf_mbx.c	SR-IOV virtchnl mailbox; omitted until SR-IOV is
			supported.

Local changes
-------------

Each change is marked with an "illumos:" comment next to the code.  All of
them treat firmware or DDP package data as untrusted: the upstream code uses
a count or length from the device or the package before it checks that the
value fits the buffer it indexes.

    ice_common.c
	ice_discover_dev_caps(), ice_discover_func_caps(): reject a
	capability count larger than the response buffer holds.

    ice_switch.c
	ice_get_initial_sw_cfg(): reject a switch configuration element
	count larger than the response buffer holds.

    ice_ddp_common.c
	ice_init_pkg_info(): reject a metadata section smaller than
	struct ice_meta_sect, and print the package name with a bounded
	length because it has no guaranteed terminator.
	ice_get_pkg_info(): reject a package count larger than
	ICE_PKG_CNT, and print firmware package names with a bounded
	length.
	ice_chk_pkg_compat(): reject a package count larger than
	ICE_PKG_CNT.

    ice_sched.c
	ice_sched_add_node(): refuse a child when the parent's children
	array (sized by max_children for its layer) is full.
	ice_sched_init_port(): reject a branch element count outside
	1..ICE_AQC_TOPO_MAX_LEVEL_NUM.
	ice_sched_query_res_alloc(): accept only a 5 or 9 layer
	topology, and require a nonzero child group size for every layer
	used as a parent, before any scheduler state is published.

usr/src/test/ice-tests/core_counts.py checks that each guard is present,
core_readme.py checks that this list matches the "illumos:" markers, and
sched_resources.py runs the scheduler admission code.

Newer upstream definitions that the driver needs are defined in the driver,
not added here.  For example, ../ice.h defines the E830 TCLAN malicious
driver detection registers that later FreeBSD and Linux autogen headers
carry.

Re-import policy
----------------

1. Copy the files from one FreeBSD commit without changes and record its
   SHA above.
2. For each local change listed above, check whether the new upstream code
   has an equivalent check.  If it does, drop the local change.  If it does
   not, apply it again with its "illumos:" comment.  Update this list.
3. Do not add new local changes for features.  Put OS glue in ice_osdep.[ch]
   or the driver, and put missing register definitions in the driver.
4. Run python3 -B usr/src/test/ice-tests/run_tests.py and a full module
   build with smatch before the change is committed.
